    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - Fixed Pose (advanced)\n\nOne depth map holds the pose; change only the prompt for another character in the same pose.\n\n1. Base + the control adapter (moss-color-depth-control, keep it at 1.0) + Turbo 8-steps v1.0, depth only,\n   8 steps, CFG 1: the pose from the map (near is white). About 3.1 s on an RTX 5090.\n2. The same latent redrawn by Base + the turbo without the adapter and without control, denoise 0.3\n   (exact): the adapter's image is soft; this pass brings back skin pores, wrinkles, veins and metal\n   detail and keeps the pose. About 3 s more.\n3. x2: RealESRGAN x2, then a MOSS pass at denoise 0.25. 18.2 s for the whole workflow, warm.\n\nMeasured (tools/RESULTS.md), three characters x 4 seeds (a knight, a potter, an astronaut), pose =\nDepth Anything V2 of the result against the map (correlation, 1 = the same depth):\n  without control 0.62, with control 0.977, after the 0.3 pass 0.976, after the x2 0.976.\n  Denoise 0.4 and 0.5 keep the pose too (0.976, 0.974) and change the picture more.\nThe map carries more than the pose: build, head and hands come from the photo (the knight got the\n  fisherman's beard; the potter, asked in her thirties, looks older in all four seeds).\n\nMaking the map: Depth Anything V2 (comfyui_controlnet_aux) or any depth tool. Look at it first:\n  it must show the silhouette. A blur with no outline is a faulty map (measured with\n  comfyui_controlnet_aux 1.1.6 on our install, see RESULTS); the control then follows only the rough layout.\nTelemetry's notes on the turbo at denoise 0.30 / 0.25 refer to its older measurements; these are in RESULTS.\n\nModels: the adapter (darask0/MOSS-Image-color-depth-control) and the turbo in models/loras,\nRealESRGAN_x2plus.pth in models/upscale_models."
   ],
